[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Encapsulation and Information Hiding in Object-Oriented Programming"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Encapsulation is one of the foundational pillars of Object-Oriented Programming (OOP). It refers to the bundling of data and the methods that operate on that data into a single unit, or class. More importantly, it restricts direct access to some of an object's components, which is a concept known as information hiding."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Core Concepts"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Data Bundling: Combining state (variables) and behavior (functions) into a single class structure."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Information Hiding: Restricting external access to internal object states to protect data integrity."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Access Modifiers: Keywords like private, protected, and public that define the visibility of class members."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Code Implementation Example"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"The following C++ example demonstrates how to encapsulate data using private member variables and expose controlled access via public getter and setter methods."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"#include <iostream>
#include <string>

class BankAccount {
private:
    double balance;

public:
    BankAccount(double initialBalance) {
        if (initialBalance >= 0) {
            balance = initialBalance;
        } else {
            balance = 0;
        }
    }

    void deposit(double amount) {
        if (amount > 0) {
            balance += amount;
        }
    }

    double getBalance() const {
        return balance;
    }
};"},{"order":10,"type":"subheading","text":"Benefits of Encapsulation"},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Control over data: Setters allow validation checks before modifying internal variables."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Flexibility and Maintainability: Internal implementation details can change without breaking external code that relies on the class."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Readability: A well-encapsulated class presents a clean, easy-to-use interface to other developers."}]
